## 2. Flagged sites

### HMENU3

**HM-1 — H1/H5, real equal-characteristic overclaim, already corrected.**

Frozen theorem statement:

> “so Ore certifies **EVERY lift**”

Frozen proof:

> “Ore (W-12 S2.3) then assigns the SAME σ to every O-lift **(not only disc ≠ 0 ones)**”

The note’s own Annex A gives the counterexample:

> “Over F_q[[t]] with p = 3, the lift F = y³ + b₀ has F′ = 3y² ≡ 0, hence gcd(F, F′) = F and disc F = 0”

Classification: **GENERAL-WITH-EDIT**. The necessary edit is exactly the annexed restriction to “every lift with `disc ≠ 0`.” This is a strict weakening, correctly acknowledged by Annex C. No count law changes.

**HM-2 — H3/H7, apparent division by 2 is only a finite-field census.**

> `A_SPLITEQ(k′) = ((q−1)(q−2)/2)q^{...}`  
> `A_INERTDEEP(k′) = (q(q−1)/2)q^{...}`

Annex B explains these as unordered-pair/Frobenius-orbit counts:

> “The first formula chooses an unordered pair of distinct nonzero residue roots. For the second, the q²−q elements of F_{q²} \ F_q form Frobenius orbits of size two”

Classification: **CLEAR-GENERAL**. No inversion of `2` in `O` or `F_q` occurs; these are integer cardinalities valid in characteristic 2.

**HM-3 — H7, half-integral raw exponents are normalized by parity progressions.**

> “the odd RAM-type parameters … carry 3/2 in RAW coordinates … which becomes integer carry 3 at the AP index u = 2i−1”

Classification: **CLEAR-GENERAL**. This is arithmetic on integer parameter sets, not division inside the DVR or extraction of roots.

**HM-4 — H6, unresolved citation scope.**

> “**Classical:** Hensel (via W12-L1), Ore/GMN order-1 (via W-12 S2.3)”

Classification: **CITE-SCOPE**. Standard Hensel lifting is available for complete DVRs in either characteristic, but no precise Ore/GMN citation or published scope is supplied here. The claim cannot receive an H6-general stamp from the pasted text alone.

**HM-5 — mixed-characteristic-only oracle explicitly non-load-bearing.**

> “Oracle: mixed-characteristic only”

and later:

> “the equal-characteristic disc = 0 lift never enters the scored set: no oracle verdict was wrong, and none was evidence about the unrestricted quantifier either”

